-#### Decoding (Bit Un-interleaving)
-The inverse operation extracts bits from the Morton code back into coordinates.
+1.  Initialize $x=0, y=0, z=0$.
+2.  For each bit index $i$ from 0 to 20:
+    a. Extract bit at position $3i$ from `morton` and place it at bit $i$ of $x$.
+    b. Extract bit at position $3i+1$ from `morton` and place it at bit $i$ of $y$.
+    c. Extract bit at position $3i+2$ from `morton` and place it at bit $i$ of $z$.
+3.  Return $(x, y, z)$.
 
-1.  Initialize $x, y, z$ to 0.
-2.  For each bit index $i$ from 0 to 20 (since $64/3 \approx 21$):
-    *   Extract the bit at position $3i$ from `morton`: `bit_x = morton & (1 << (3*i))`
-    *   Extract the bit at position $3i+1$ from `morton`: `bit_y = morton & (1 << (3*i+1))`
-    *   Extract the bit at position $3i+2$ from `morton`: `bit_z = morton & (1 << (3*i+2))`
-    *   Shift bits back to position $i$:
-        $$ x \ |= \ (bit\_x \gg ((3i + 0) - i)) $$
-        $$ y \ |= \ (bit\_y \gg ((3i + 1) - i)) $$
-        $$ z \ |= \ (bit\_z \gg ((3i + 2) - i)) $$
-3.  Return $(x, y, z)$ [S7, unofficial].
+*Formula:*
+$$ x = \bigvee_{i=0}^{20} \left( (morton \& (1 \ll (3i))) \gg i \right) $$
+$$ y = \bigvee_{i=0}^{20} \left( (morton \& (1 \ll (3i+1))) \gg i \right) $$
+$$ z = \bigvee_{i=0}^{20} \left( (morton \& (1 \ll (3i+2))) \gg i \right) $$
